Title: The Welcome
Order: 23
Production Code: 1x23

INT. LIVINGSTON HALL - DIANTHE'S ROOM - NIGHT

AMB: distant, then swelling, ceremonial music no living guest can place

[[Dianthe Lusk]] is dying, tended by [[Hannah]], through a long gray day and into the night. [[Aubrey Livingston]] has fled the house, unable to face what he's done. Sound builds in the corridors — organ, harp, drums, a chorus of thousands where no one stands.

DIANTHE LUSK
(rising up, radiant, seeing what no one else can)
I see them — the glorious band! Candace! Semiramis! Solomon and David and the great kings of old! Beethoven — Mozart — let me kneel to you!

The vision passes. She goes rigid, listening for something else now.

DIANTHE LUSK (CONT'D)
Carriage wheels. Do you hear them? They're at the crossing — hasten, hasten — they call me home.

AUNT HANNAH
(soft, to the room)
One comes who is de instrument ob de Lord.

Wheels on gravel, at last, for real. Footsteps on the stairs, closer, faster.

The door opens. [[Reuel Briggs]] is in the room.

With one wild cry of joy, Dianthe crosses to him and is folded into his arms — and, still smiling, dies there, silently, her guilt and grief both spent.
